# Cramapple Technical & AI Architecture Specification

This blueprint defines the infrastructural data schema, low-latency pipeline routing, and anti-hallucination guardrails powering the PassTo/Cramapple scoring engine.

---

## 1. PostgreSQL Schema (Supabase DDL Layer)

The relational engine stores strict structured outputs under strict Row-Level Security (RLS) policies. This schema decouples the core context-pinned rubrics from volatile student telemetry logs.

```sql
-- Enable Vector Extension for Pinned Content Ingestion
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

-- Master Curriculum Context Table
CREATE TABLE public.context_pinned_rubrics (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    unit_id INT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    unit_title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    rubric_payload JSONB NOT NULL, -- Holds explicit Define, Explain, Predict targets
    target_max_points INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 3,
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Student Mastery & Diagnostic Execution Ledger
CREATE TABLE public.student_mastery_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    student_id UUID NOT NULL,
    unit_id INT NOT NULL REFERENCES public.context_pinned_rubrics(unit_id),
    points_earned INT NOT NULL,
    max_points INT NOT NULL,
    mastery_tier VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL, -- 'Score 3', 'Score 4', 'Score 5'
    is_logic_gap BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    raw_response_payload JSONB NOT NULL, -- Stores structural D, E, P inputs
    diagnostic_feedback JSONB NOT NULL,  -- Stores structural protocolActionPlan
    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Enable RLS on telemetry layers
ALTER TABLE public.student_mastery_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Students can only access their own mastery logs"
    ON public.student_mastery_logs
    FOR SELECT
    USING (auth.uid() = student_id);
